=== Miy_2H_01 ===
// player walks up, at fountain in town
// Miya is sitting on bench
You notice Miya sitting by the fountain, but she looks lost in thought. #speaker:none #emotion:none
...
Oh hey *player*! #speaker:Miya #emotion:neutral
Sorry, I didn't see you walk up.
Come on over and have a seat, I promise I don't bite. #emotion:happy
// player walks over
-> END

=== Miy_2H_02 ===
So how's your day been, *player*? #speaker:Miya #emotion:happy
Oh! I saw your farm the other day, seems like it's coming along pretty well!
Not that I would know that much about plants... #emotion:xd
But I could tell that they were nice and happy. #emotion:happy
For a while you two sit in silence. Not an awkward silence, just two people simply taking a rest. #speaker:none #emotion:none
...
Hey *player*, do you know the story behind this fountain? #speaker:Miya #emotion:neutral
Apparently it was built in honor of my grandma, Catia Ziegler. #emotion:happy
She was the first surrogate mother of the settlement. #emotion:neutral
You know, having a surrogate mother makes things a lot easier for the gene pool, population growth, things like that.
Sorry I forget, you already know most of this stuff... #emotion:xd
Anyways, the settlement knew just how much of a toll it took on her. #emotion:neutral
So they built this in her honor. #emotion:happy
I mean, just think about it. She gave birth to nine of us... #emotion:neutral
The amount of bravery and selflessness she must've had... I can't even imagine... #emotion:sad
Say... *player*... you would've known her, right? #emotion:neutral
Tell me, what was she like?
Well, she was actually the designated <color={red}>Logistics Officer</color>. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
So she made sure that everyone had enough food and supplies.
But she also knew that she was a top candidate to be a surrogate mother in the event the incubator wasn't available.
...Incubator? #speaker:Miya #emotion:neutral
Well it's way more complex than a simple incubator, that's just what we called it. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
But it essentially would've allowed us humans to repopulate without needing a surrogate mother. Instead it would all be done in a small chamber.
That's... I can't even imagine it. I guess there's probably a lot of things on Earth that are just science fiction to us now. #speaker:Miya #emotion:sad
But... tell me more about my grandmother. What was her personality like? #emotion:neutral

*   [Describe her as caring, nurturing]
    Well... I can totally see her taking on a role as important as a surrogate mother. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Miya/5
    She was always the mother of the group, breaking up arguments and making sure people were taken care of.
    And she loved to tell everyone her dreams of eventually having a big family on Raea.
    So she really was perfect for the job in a sense.
    That's good to know. Based on what you and Charlotte said, it doesn't seem like she was forced to do it or anything. #speaker:Miya #emotion:happy
    
*   [Describe her as friendly, outgoing]
    Well... she was always one of the first people to say hi to you. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Miya/3
    She'd always make sure everyone's voice was heard, and would always put others first.
    She was a real leader in that sense.
    Wow, that's awesome to hear, *player*. #speaker:Miya #emotion:xd
    Although, I'm definitely not be as outgoing as her. But I did always look up to her as a leader. #emotion:happy
    
*   [Describe her as chatty, unauthentic]
    Well... she was definitely the chatterbox of the group. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Miya/-3
    She couldn't stand when she wasn't the center of attention, or when someone had taken the spotlight from her.
    That's probably why she always butted heads with Atkins, since he was voted to be the leader instead of her.
    Oh... I didn't know any of that about her. #speaker:Miya #emotion:neutral
    Charlotte was friends with her and has only told me good things...
    Guess that's hard to hear that she wasn't who I thought she was... #emotion:sad
    
-   I guess I only ask because my mom, Eva, always compares me to her. #speaker:Miya #emotion:neutral
I guess there's more than one reason for that, seeing how I'm in line to be the next surrogate mother... #emotion:sad
(She doesn't seem too thrilled about that at all) #speaker:*player* #emotion:none
-> END

=== Miy_2H_03 ===
But... for now I should get going. #speaker:Miya #emotion:happy
Can't be away from the hospital too long or Kane will find out. #emotion:xd
But thanks for talking to me, *player*. #emotion:happy
I really appreciate you telling me about my grandma.
See you around! #emotion:xd
-> END

=== Miy_4H_01 ===

According to the story, the leader back then, Mayor Atkins, got into a big fight with Marco, another one of the Founders. #emotion:neutral
It was big enough of a fight that nobody really knew what was going to happen to the settlement.
I don't know what the fight was about, but 
-> END

=== Miy_4H_02 ===
// about Miku?
Well... I always saw her as a nice, soft-spoken girl. #speaker:*player* #emotion:none #relation_pts:Miya/2
    She would often prefer to be off on her own, watering her plants or reading in the courtyard.
    Don't get me wrong, she loved to have her friends around her, but she also equally liked her space.
    I guess I'm trying to say she was one of the few introverts among the selected crew.
    \*Giggle* That's how Charlotte talks about her as well. Says that's why they were friends... because my grandma was the only person who could be quiet and listen. #speaker:Miya #emotion:happy
-> END
